<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carolingian civil war</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">840–843</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carolingian civil war (840–843) was fought among the sons of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Frankish empire</a> after his death in 840. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair I</a>, who claimed the whole empire, was defeated at Fontenoy in 841 by his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, who confirmed their alliance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaths-of-strasbourg">Oaths of Strasbourg</a> in 842. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> (843) divided the empire into three kingdoms, the roots of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carolingian-civil-war.jpg" alt="Carolingian civil war" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_the_Bald_-_detail_from_Codex_Aureus_of_Saint_Emmeram.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
